  "about": "The animation libraries tools/anim draws on: where each archive is, its exact bytes and sha256, its licence, the in-place glb inside it and the length of every action (frames at fps). UAL 1 and UAL 2 share one 65-bone skeleton (same bone names and rest pose), so a clip may take its base from one and a layer from the other. `pnpm anim fetch` downloads, checks and unpacks them into tools/.cache/anim/lib/; nothing of them is committed.",
